    "summary": "Countrified Garcia, sweet organ, strong jams & Baby Blue finale",
    "blurb": "Garcia’s countrified guitar shines on Black Peter and the blues‑heavy set while Pigpen’s organ adds warmth throughout. The Other One, Dancin’ In The Street and the China Cat Sunflower→I Know You Rider segue are highlights, making this a solid late‑'69 performance.",
    "review": "On December 5, 1969 at the Fillmore West the Dead delivered a quintessential late‑60s set that balances country‑tinged storytelling with exploratory jams. Jerry Garcia’s guitar takes on a countrified tone—pedal‑steel‑like licks ripple through Black Peter and the tender “It’s All Over Now Baby Blue” closing, while Pigpen’s organ provides a sweet, ever‑present backdrop. The second half erupts with classic improvisational peaks: The Other One rolls into an expansive jam, Dancin’ In The Street bursts with energy, and the seamless China Cat Sunflower→I Know You Rider segue showcases tight interplay. Though the opening “Me And My Uncle” and “Casey Jones” suffer from a loose mic plug in the soundboard source, the overall performance is cohesive, melodic, and captures the mellow yet adventurous vibe of the era.",
